    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "i used to think everything depended on being the best. like if i wasn't going to be top tier, there was no point in even trying. i just hit this wall today. i realized i'm just... okay. i'll always just be okay. it feels like i've been playing a game for years just to realize i'm a NPC in my own life. what's even the point of grinding through decades of mediocrity?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It's a huge relief to finally stop chasing an impossible standard, but that realization is also a heavy weight to carry. Being \"okay\" is a perfectly valid, and often deeply satisfying, place to be, and it's not a failure. You don't have to be a protagonist to have a meaningful life; the point is in the quiet, small moments, not in the grand, unattainable achievements. Give yourself permission to just *be* in the middle, and see what that feels like.",
      "source": "target",
